## 7. Live Tele-Mentoring & Streaming Workflow (AWS IVS)

When a trainee is conducting an ultrasound scan in the VR headset, an instructor can join in real-time to watch the plane acquisition sweep, probe orientation, and provide tele-mentoring guidance.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Trainee as Trainee (VR Headset)
    participant Server as Express Backend (streamingService.js)
    participant AWS_IVS as AWS IVS Real-Time (Stages)
    actor Instructor as Instructor (Web Dashboard)

    Trainee->>Server: POST /api/v1/streaming/sessions (Start Session, Role: Trainee)
    Server->>AWS_IVS: CreateStageCommand(StageName)
    AWS_IVS-->>Server: Return Stage ARN
    Server->>AWS_IVS: CreateParticipantTokenCommand (Publisher Capabilities)
    AWS_IVS-->>Server: Return Publisher Token
    Server-->>Trainee: Return Stage ARN + Publisher Token

    Trainee->>AWS_IVS: Join Stage as WebRTC Publisher (Ultrasound Video Stream)

    Instructor->>Server: GET /api/v1/streaming/sessions/active (List Active Sessions)
    Server-->>Instructor: Active Trainee Sessions in Instructor's Batch
    Instructor->>Server: POST /api/v1/streaming/sessions/:id/join (Role: Instructor)
    Server->>AWS_IVS: CreateParticipantTokenCommand (Viewer / Subscriber Capabilities)
    AWS_IVS-->>Server: Return Viewer Token
    Server-->>Instructor: Return Viewer Token

    Instructor->>AWS_IVS: Join Stage as Viewer (Receive Ultrasound Video Stream)
    Note over Trainee,Instructor: Live Realtime Ultrasound Feed & Tele-Mentoring Guidance

    Trainee->>Server: DELETE /api/v1/streaming/sessions/:id (End Scan)
    Server->>AWS_IVS: DeleteStageCommand
    Server-->>Trainee: Session Ended
    Server-->>Instructor: Notification: Stream Closed
```

